      "text": "To solve the problem, we first need to determine Jana's walking speed in miles per minute. We know that Jana takes 24 minutes to walk one mile. Therefore, her speed is:\n\nSpeed = \\(\\frac{\\text{Distance}}{\\text{Time}} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}}\\).\n\nNext, we determine the distance Jana will walk in 10 minutes by using her speed and the time interval in minutes. We multiply her speed by the given time to get the distance:\n\nDistance = Speed \\times Time = \\(\\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}\\).\n\nLet's calculate the distance using Python.\n```python\n# Given values\ntime_for_one_mile = 24  # minutes\ntime_given = 10  # minutes\n\n# Calculate the distance Jana walks in the given time\ndistance_walked = time_given * (1 / time_for_one_mile)\ndistance_rounded = round(distance_walked, 1)\n\nprint(distance_rounded)\n```\n```output\n0.4\n```\nJana will walk \\(\\boxed{0.4}\\) miles in 10 minutes.",
